A broad woman kneels in a tended row of the Glut, pressing a seed into the dark with both thumbs, unhurried.
"Mind the row. Something true is coming up out of it, and true things come up slow."
"Hearthward Ona Bramblekind. I raise the soft creed's proof: that love is a method, not a mood."
"Feed them right, raise them kind, and the bond does three jobs for you. That's not sentiment, climber. That's husbandry."
[She turns the seed in your palm so the six faint ridges catch the light.]
"The six-petal isn't stronger. It doesn't fight better. It's just true, and ours, and it took us generations to coax up out of the dark of the blood."
"Old Garran will offer you a shortcut. Garran always does. The shortcut works — that's the trouble with it."
"Take the seed. Raise it the long way. And when Garran smiles at you, remember whose row you're standing in."
